whelk (0.3.2-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Session detection asks the compositor when no variable names one, so a bar
    started by a service unit or a login shell keeps its window and menu modules.
  * The detected session, and what proved it, is logged once at startup.

 -- Josep Bigorra <jjbigorra@gmail.com>  Thu, 12 Nov 2026 22:00:00 +0100

whelk (0.3.1-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * The Nix expression runs the Guile theme test too, and refuses to package a
    tree that already carries a build directory.

 -- Josep Bigorra <jjbigorra@gmail.com>  Thu, 12 Nov 2026 21:00:00 +0100

whelk (0.3.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * A session layer: niri, sway and X11 each answer "what is in front" and
    "close it" in their own way, and the focused window, the global menu and
    its shortcuts work on all three.
  * An X11 dock fallback: a bar reserves its edge with EWMH struts.
  * Graceful degradation where layer-shell is missing (GNOME Wayland): surfaces
    are ordinary windows and the launcher, panels and notifications still work.

 -- Josep Bigorra <jjbigorra@gmail.com>  Thu, 12 Nov 2026 20:00:00 +0100

whelk (0.2.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * A macOS-shaped bar: the shell's own menu and a global menu that reads an
    application's menubar over D-Bus and synthesizes one when it exports none.
  * Bar themes: era-inspired and community palettes, brand-free names.
  * The launcher searches every file and folder under $HOME, caches and
    repositories skipped, ranked by name and path.
  * A vertical bar keeps its last group on screen and reserves the width it
    paints.

 -- Josep Bigorra <jjbigorra@gmail.com>  Thu, 12 Nov 2026 19:10:00 +0100

whelk (0.1.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Initial release: bars on any edge with status, media, system and tray
    modules; a launcher with app, window, run, calc, file, web and menu modes;
    an org.freedesktop.Notifications daemon with toasts and a notification
    centre; and a Wi-Fi and Bluetooth panel whose typed password replaces the
    saved key without ever appearing on a command line.

 -- Josep Bigorra <jjbigorra@gmail.com>  Thu, 12 Nov 2026 18:30:00 +0000
